# Step 3b kernel-config delta: enable MP-table parsing.
#
# Human-readable RECORD of the change (the authoritative config is
# microvm-kernel-x86_64-6.1.config, which build_kernel.sh copies to .config and
# runs through olddefconfig — that strips comments, hence this file, matching
# the step2a-container.config convention).
#
# One-line change vs the Step-2 config:
CONFIG_X86_MPPARSE=y
#
# Rationale:
#   MPPARSE required for MP-table interrupt enumeration; guest was silently in
#   virtual-wire mode through Step 2.
#
# Detail: the base Firecracker microvm config shipped with X86_MPPARSE OFF.
# Because it is `bool "Enable MPS table" if ACPI` (ACPI=y here) it stayed a
# user-visible option and olddefconfig honored the explicit "not set". With the
# parser absent, arch/x86/kernel/mpparse.c is not compiled, so `smp_found_config`
# could never be set (we provide NO ACPI RSDP/MADT by design). Per
# __apic_intr_mode_select() (arch/x86/kernel/apic/apic.c), !smp_found_config
# forces APIC_VIRTUAL_WIRE_NO_CONFIG -> IO-APIC setup skipped and the LAPIC
# timer is never registered (guest ticks off the i8253 PIT; /proc/interrupts
# LOC stays 0). Step 3b needs the guest on the LAPIC TSC-deadline clockevent, so
# the MP table must actually be parsed: this option makes that possible, and the
# MP table itself (src/mptable.rs) carries the IRQ0->IOAPIC-pin-2 override so the
# parsed routing matches the conventional PC layout.
#
# Reproducibility: the rebuilt vmlinux is a NEW pinned artifact; its sha256 is
# recorded in guest/kernel/vmlinux-6.1.128.sha256. From Step 3b on, the
# reproducibility unit is the (vmlinux sha256 + initramfs sha256) pair.
